KNOWNBUG
gated_clock_issue2366.sv
--top gated --bound 6
^\[gated\.p_hold\] .*: PROVED up to bound 6$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The only use of clk as a clock is the clocking event of the property,
which the parser discards. Hence clk is not identified as the base clock
of gclk, and the always construct is not gated.
